00000, h=1000` makes `4·w·h ≡ +294967296 (mod 2³²)`, so the C really does process pixels. I re-scoped rows 7/8 and added `ERRORS.md` row 20 / `CONFIGS.md` row 27 for the mixed-sign wrap-to-positive cases.\n\n## Phases B–D results\n\n- **51 tests**, all passing, ~150k C-vs-Rust `.so` invocations per run. Both libraries always via `dlopen`/`dlsym` — never a direct Rust call, so the `#[no_mangle]` wrapper is under test.\n- **Feature combos:** `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` and `c_src` has no `option()`/`#ifdef`, so the complete set is the single empty combination — verified with both `--no-default-features` and `--all-features`, and Phases B–C re-run against **dev and release** `.so`s.\n- **Extra assurance:** Rust matches C built at `-O0/-O1/-O2/-O3/-Ofast`; matches with `-C target-cpu=native` and `-C debug-assertions=on`; the arithmetic core is verified **exhaustively** over all 65 536 `(colour, alpha)` pairs, with `cfg28` proving the float→int conversion can never reach a saturation path.\n- Full clean run (`rm -rf target c_src/build && ./run_all.sh`) → ALL CHECKS PASSED.\n\nOnly `Cargo.toml` (added `libloading` to `[dev-dependencies]`), `src/lib.rs`, and new root/test files changed; `c_src/` sources retain their original mtimes."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1096,"cache_read_input_tokens":160355,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1096,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6a65eb01-3a90-4dd7-9913-8fac91b28eb5","uuid":"0fe69f2c-4f36-4803-8bbd-b1a9aaea18c0","timestamp":"2026-08-19T14:31:08.317Z"}
